      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I understand the test. The `factory_of_Instant` test is simple, but the file is cluttered with many unused data providers and helper methods irrelevant to this single test. I'll write a clean version that removes all the noise and adds meaningful context.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file strips out all unused data providers and helper methods unrelated to the single `factory_of_Instant` test, introduces a named constant `MJD_UNIX_EPOCH` with an explanatory comment, and adds inline comments that explain what `Instant.ofEpochSecond(0, 2)` represents and why the expected MJD (40587) and nano-of-day (2) are correct."
